Drink exactly one large glass of warm water every hour for the next four hours. By aggressively flooding your circulatory system with fluid, you mechanically dilute the concentration of rigid, sickled cells in your blood, physically helping to break the microscopic blockages.

Keep the room temperature consistently warm and utilize a heating pad on the painful thighs. By applying localized heat, you force the surrounding blood vessels to dilate, allowing the trapped sickled cells to finally flow through.
